<title>USA: USDA Jan 10 world grain highlights.</title>
<headline>USDA Jan 10 world grain highlights.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agriculture Department on Friday estimated Brazilian soybean production in 1996/97 at 26.00 million tonnes and Argentine bean production at 13.00 million, both unchanged from last month's estimates.</p>
<p>USDA left China's major crop production estimates unchanged, but lowered its wheat import estimate to 4.00 million tonnes and raised soybean meal imports to 1.9 million tonnes.</p>
<p>In other noteworthy changes, USDA lowered Canada's wheat export estimate to 16.0 million tonnes, raised Australian wheat exports to 14.0 million, and raised Argentina's corn exports to 8.25 million tonnes.  </p>
<p>World grain crops will total 1,840.59 million tonnes in 1996/97, down from last month's estimate of 1.841.78 million tonnes and above last year's 1,703.25 million. Wheat was pegged at 579.09 million tonnes, coarse grains at 884.66 million and rice at 376.84 million. Oilseeds were forecast at 255.31 million tonnes and cotton at 86.37 million bales.  </p>
